<title>USA: U.S. judge okays use of 16 Brown papers at trial.</title>
<headline>U.S. judge okays use of 16 Brown papers at trial.</headline>
<dateline>MIAMI 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Plaintiff lawyers may use at next week's secondhand-smoke trial 16 confidential documents taken from a law firm by a paralegal working for Brown &amp; Williamson, the U.S. tobacco arm of B.A.T Industries, a Florida judge ruled on Tuesday.</p>
<p>But Dade County Court Judge Robert Kaye said 12 other Brown &amp; Williamson documents plaintiff lawyers Stanley and Susan Rosbenblatt had sought may not be used at the trial scheduled to begin on Monday.</p>
</text>
